--Data Types in SQL

SQL data types define what kind of data a column can store. Choosing the correct data type helps maintain data accuracy, consistency, and efficient storage.

📚 Main Categories
Category	                      Used For		                      Examples
🔢 Numeric		                  Numbers		                        INT, BIGINT, DECIMAL, FLOAT
🔤 Character/String	            Text		                          CHAR, VARCHAR, TEXT
📅 Date & Time	                Dates and times		                DATE, TIME, DATETIME, TIMESTAMP
✅ Boolean	                    True/False values		              BOOLEAN, BIT
🧮 Binary	Binary                data		                          BINARY, VARBINARY
📦 Other/Specialized	          Database-specific data	          JSON, XML, UUID

QUICK REFERENCE   

💠 DATATYPE        📦 STORES                    💾 STORAGE       📏 RANGE / LIMIT
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

🔢 INT             Whole numbers                4 bytes          -2,147,483,648 to
                                                                  2,147,483,647

